	"_about": "Decor (see Decor, DecorRoom, DecorateMode). The shop sells shop_per_day items a day, picked from those whose tier (stars needed) has been reached. An item: kind is floor or wall, size is its [width, depth] in meters on the floor, points count toward the Decor area of the star rating, set (optional) names a set. parts are what it looks like: { box: [x, y, z] } or { cylinder: [radius, height] } with a color, or { model: path, size: [x, y, z] }, each with at: [x, y, z] (the bottom middle of the part, from the item's bottom middle). ALL OF THIS IS PLACEHOLDER ART AND PLACEHOLDER PRICES. Scoring: each item id counts up to max_copies times, a category is worth at most category_cap points (so one category can't do it all), and a whole set placed adds set_points. grid is the floor's squares (cell meters each; min and max are the middles of the corner squares): floor decor always fills whole squares, so a floor item's size should be whole squares; keep_clear rectangles [x1, z1, x2, z2] keep the customers' lanes, the tables, the line, the doors and the pass free, and nothing goes within station_gap meters of a station. wall_spots are where wall decor hangs (turn in degrees).",
